<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Herbert Samuel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1870–1963</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Herbert Samuel, 1st Viscount Samuel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Herbert Samuel was a British Liberal politician and the first practising Jew in a British cabinet. In July 1920 he became the first High Commissioner for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a>, replacing the military Occupied Enemy Territory Administration with a civil government. He served until 1925, during the early years of conflict between the Jewish and Arab national movements.</p></div>
